{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what","id":1494111,"title":"New Orleans is the new capital of the Sabbat, & the Cathari have been purged, now what?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-01T16:27:41-07:00","id":1494111,"title":"New Orleans is the new capital of the Sabbat, & the Cathari have been purged, now what?","content":"I constructed a campaign that started with the siege of New Orleans. Once New Orleans was captured, the Grand Inquisitor of the Sabbat declared New Orleans the new Sabbat capital, abolished the Regent position, declared the Sabbat Inquisition to be the governing body of the Sabbat with herself the Grand Inquisitor on top, and declared the Cathari Demagogues and all those loyal to them heretical and began a purge of Cathari.<br /> <br /> There's still some diplomatic stuff to see if the Noddist leadership will back this purge. If not, the resultant civil war will be long and bloody. If the Noddist leadership DOES back the Grand Inquisitor, then the civil war will be short and little more than a large scale wild hunt.<br /> <br /> After that, though, I don't really have any plans. It may well be that this is simply the natural endpoint of the campaign. However, the players are having fun and like their characters, so I'd like to continue if possible. So I came here to ask for help brainstorming for continued story ideas. Thank you in advance for any suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T19:08:32-07:00","id":1494116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what#post1494111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I constructed a campaign that started with the siege of New Orleans. Once New Orleans was captured, the Grand Inquisitor of the Sabbat declared New Orleans the new Sabbat capital, abolished the Regent position, declared the Sabbat Inquisition to be the governing body of the Sabbat with herself the Grand Inquisitor on top, and declared the Cathari Demagogues and all those loyal to them heretical and began a purge of Cathari.<br /> <br /> There's still some diplomatic stuff to see if the Noddist leadership will back this purge. If not, the resultant civil war will be long and bloody. If the Noddist leadership DOES back the Grand Inquisitor, then the civil war will be short and little more than a large scale wild hunt.<br /> <br /> After that, though, I don't really have any plans. It may well be that this is simply the natural endpoint of the campaign. However, the players are having fun and like their characters, so I'd like to continue if possible. So I came here to ask for help brainstorming for continued story ideas. Thank you in advance for any suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, how solid is the Sabbat's position in the rest of Louisiana? Because if they don't have a good number of neighboring domains on their side i can see this Grand Inquisitor having something of a problem sustaining its power base. What are the other notable sabbat leading figures, supportive, neutral, antagonistic to account for, both in their vicinity or far away enclaves? How is the situation in Mexico city, Montreal and other places supposedly in the grasp of the Sword of Caine?<br /> <br /> Yes, acess to planes can help with sidestepping distance and border issues, but to a definitely limited degree - long-distance communications can matter and help immensely with building alliances but ultimately every city or metropolitan area is an &quot;isle of herds&quot; of its own to be managed, preserved or exploited according to local powers' needs.<br /> <br /> So on short run, who must be dealt with in New Orleans - is the city fully in the Sabbat hands or are there any Camarilla or independent enclaves that might prove something of a nuisance or actual threat? What packs are in the city and who leads them? How strongly are they in the Grand Inquisitor's support, against it or on the fence? And what might it take to make either of these groups change sides?<br /> <br /> And all of that applies to the PCs too - are they loyal to Grand Inquisitor or could they end up supporting someone else, or even themselves, to supplanting it and/or the Cathari? Any major canon Sabbat NPCs still around that could become a factor either way?<br /> <br /> Any random kindred with Dominate 4-5 <i>that might turn everything on its head</i> by rewiring individual loyalties according to its own mysterious agendas &amp; tastes?<br /> Draw out a good map of the characters at play in the &quot;field of operations&quot; and the possibilties will present themselves, i think.<br /> <br /> With that done it becomes just a matter of applying the same principle in ever greater scopes.<br /> <br /> Who would be against the abolition of the Regent role and might fight for its preservation, for selfish self-interest, selflessly pragmatic or other reasons? Who would be in favor, but calls bull$#it on the Grand Inquisitor as just a Regent under another name? Where do the other paths stand - and how might those in Evil Revelations, service to the Antediluvians or a number of other secret camps with a vested interest in seeing the Inquisition take a nosedive exploit the situation?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what about extra complications like mortal hunter groups, lupines, the Technocracy or other groups with a possible vested interest in the well-being of people or the society? Large numbers of Sabbat in the same are usually not exactly conductive to a happy, peaceful and prosperous way of life for the mortal herd, so there's definite potential for extra strife to spring from any - or all - of those sources, with more drama &amp; action rising from its resolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-01-2022, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T03:10:20-07:00","id":1494127,"title":"","content":"Obviously contention point is the Regent and the pricus council.<br /> <br /> The other issues I can infrastructure restoration, the status of the clans/Bloodlines and sect reaction to 2nd inquisition how and what needs to be done.<br /> <br /> Couple of recent changes I've done:<br /> In my own game I've had the Sabbat set up boot camps for mass embraces and pack formation. This allows the monitoring of shovelheads and any problem candidates to be filtered out.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat take the silence if the blood more seriously and most territories have a Bishop of silence for that task.<br /> <br /> Clan ravnos is now a de facto Sabbat clan due to Liberal sect embracing policies and main clan decimation in the week of nightmares. They act as a pragmatic counterweight to the power hungry lasombra and weird tzmisce.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-02-2022, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T04:22:36-07:00","id":1494130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what?p=1494127#post1494127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously contention point is the Regent and the prices council.<br /> <br /> The other issues I can infrastructure restoration, the status of the clans/Bloodlines and sect reaction to 2nd inquisition how and what needs to be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Which influential individuals support the old Regent or the choosing of a new one - who is (or was, if destroyed) the Regent in that chronicle, in fact? - which ones are in favor of the Sabbat Inquisition takeover, which ones support the abolition of the title, but support another replacement instead or <i>no substitute whatsoever</i> and letting a mix of Prisci Council and Cardinals make any general policy decisions collectively, if needed? All of these and more may come up as ad hoc factions that were mostly simmering under the status quo until the current situation sparked their interest. Who could become allies of convenience or rising rivals, well, the PCs actions might partly help in deciding that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what?p=1494127#post1494127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my own game I've had the Sabbat set up boot camps for mass embraces and pack formation. This allows the monitoring of shovelheads and any problem candidates to be filtered out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to kind of defeat the point of &quot;shovelheads as disposable cannon fodder&quot; imho, but at the same time i can see a number of loyalists and path zealots going into &quot;spiritual wellbeing over short-term victories&quot; bender, so it can certainly make sense. In fact contention over such an issue can make another factional knot for the PCs - or any rival faction - to try to get supporters by dealing with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what?p=1494127#post1494127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat take the silence if the blood more seriously and most territories have a Bishop of silence for that task.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would probably go with a group of Templars of Silence instead, but the idea is sound indeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what?p=1494127#post1494127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clan ravnos is now a de facto Sabbat clan due to Liberal sect embracing policies and main clan decimation in the week of nightmares. They act as a pragmatic counterweight to the power hungry lasombra and weird tzmisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this makes such an entertaining twist of fate it almost tempts to adopt the Week of Nightmares in my games. Almost.<br /> <br /> <br /> And now back to the basics....<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\">CajunKhan</a></b>, how is your version of New Orleans, who was involved in the city's siege, any canon figures or heavy hitters of your own creation, beside the Grand Inquisitor i guess?<br /> Are there any Camarilla or independent kindred still around and how active of a resistance do they offer?<br /> Any turncoats now turned covenmembers or packmates?<br /> What kindred already had something of a presence in local <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">vodousaint community, Setites, Samedi, Serpents of Light, others?<br /> <br /> How does Montreal's <i>Perfecti</i>, that not only seemed to be quite respected locally, but were driving something of a schism within followers of the path even within canon, fit into this? (Feel free yo ignore that if you're not familiar with or interested in Montreal by Night)</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-02-2022, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T04:38:19-07:00","id":1494131,"title":"","content":"If the Sabbat is in doubt then its...War with the Camarilla/Ancients!<br /> <br /> It seems that if the Sabbat has settled its internal issues its time to look outward towards the sect's external enemies to keep the sect from creating new internael conflicts and try to steer the momentum from the internal strife to more production purposes (for the sect and its leaders).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T11:59:11-07:00","id":1494144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what?p=1494131#post1494131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Sabbat is in doubt then its...War with the Camarilla/Ancients!<br /> <br /> It seems that if the Sabbat has settled its internal issues its time to look outward towards the sect's external enemies to keep the sect from creating new internael conflicts and try to steer the momentum from the internal strife to more production purposes (for the sect and its leaders).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the matter is that, from what is said right out in the OP, internal issues are <b><i>still quite far from really settled</i></b> and the main question in the air would be &quot;can we make this civil war a short one, or will it be a long and very damaging one?&quot;, very dependant in whose loyalties each side can or not gather for this big fight (not to mention other factions taking the lead on the conflict &amp; gaining recognition from the greater part of the sect instead).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-02-2022, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T14:08:42-07:00","id":1494153,"title":"","content":"Organise the Gehenna Crusaders who weren't targeted. They need to know that they aren't next, that the Sabbat is still committed to the liberation of cainites from the antediluvians and not ruled by an elite that's protecting the latter by starting civil wars. Other path followers will also question when the Inquisition will decide that they need to be purged, so their place in the Sabbat needs to be validated somehow. Otherwise, there's going to be a &quot;True Sword of Caine&quot; forming on one hand and a Circle of the Crone-esque group of spiritual Loyalists on the other, leaving or fighting the new order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T18:19:39-07:00","id":1494166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what?p=1494144#post1494144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, the matter is that, from what is said right out in the OP, internal issues are <b><i>still quite far from really settled</i></b> and the main question in the air would be &quot;can we make this civil war a short one, or will it be a long and very damaging one?&quot;, very dependant in whose loyalties each side can or not gather for this big fight (not to mention other factions taking the lead on the conflict &amp; gaining recognition from the greater part of the sect instead).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see that quote or something like it in the OP. The closest you get is that the new Grand Inquisitor boss needs &quot;some diplomacy&quot; to get the purge and actions reactively approved by the Noddist leadership. That's not at all &quot;far from settled&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T19:09:19-07:00","id":1494169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what?p=1494130#post1494130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. Which influential individuals support the old Regent or the choosing of a new one - who is (or was, if destroyed) the Regent in that chronicle, in fact? - which ones are in favor of the Sabbat Inquisition takeover, which ones support the abolition of the title, but support another replacement instead or <i>no substitute whatsoever</i> and letting a mix of Prisci Council and Cardinals make any general policy decisions collectively, if needed? All of these and more may come up as ad hoc factions that were mostly simmering under the status quo until the current situation sparked their interest. Who could become allies of convenience or rising rivals, well, the PCs actions might partly help in deciding that.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my world, Regent Melinda Galbraith became increasingly erratic and isolated, largely abandoning control of the sect a couple of decades ago and then vanishing entirely. As she become dramatically less interested in ruling, Cathari demagogues mostly gained control over the fractious sect. The Cathari demagogues appealed to the most hedonistic desires of the masses. Under their influence, the Cathari path swelled enormously in numbers, because they raised their shovelheads to True Sabbat status in a tiny fraction of the time of most Paths. They basically raised their shovelheads to True Sabbat status the moment they displayed clear devotion to the Path, ignoring any requirements of military discipline and competence. They also encouraged incredibly reckless, but popular, behavior, essentially turning the Sabbat into a bunch of incompetent psychopathic hedonists.<br /> <br /> This resulted in the loss of considerable amounts of Sabbat territory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does Montreal's <i>Perfecti</i>, that not only seemed to be quite respected locally, but were driving something of a schism within followers of the path even within canon, fit into this? (Feel free yo ignore that if you're not familiar with or interested in Montreal by Night)[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR] </div> </div> </div>Montreal was lost. Many blame Cathari incompetence and recklessness for this loss. What has made it much worse is the clumsy propaganda the Cathari demagogues put out afterwards, claiming that this was a good thing, that the Sabbat had evolved beyond the need for territory, and that the Sabbat was more dangerous than ever without territory. This propaganda was so blatantly absurd and such a ridiculous insult to the intelligence of most older Sabbat that it aroused a &quot;let them eat cake&quot; level of F-YOUUUU!!!!! from the followers of more disciplined paths. Only the sheer numbers of the Cathari prevented an immediate civil war.<br /> <br /> The Grand Inquisitor used this widespread hatred to promote her own agenda. She believes the Sabbat should be a disciplined nation and a safe haven for those vampires that reject humanity and desire to advance spiritually on Paths of Enlightenment. As such, it needs to reconquer a reasonably large amount of territory, secure the borders of that territory, and purge those elements that either oppose those two goals, or threaten to cause juicebag stampedes with their idiocy.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 10-02-2022, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T01:35:07-07:00","id":1494187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what?p=1494131#post1494131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Sabbat is in doubt then its...War with the Camarilla/Ancients!<br /> <br /> It seems that if the Sabbat has settled its internal issues its time to look outward towards the sect's external enemies to keep the sect from creating new internael conflicts and try to steer the momentum from the internal strife to more production purposes (for the sect and its leaders).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, going back to the OP, my attention was kind of drawn to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If <b>not</b>, <i>the resultant civil war will be long and bloody</i>. </div> </div> </div>So, yeah, brink of civil war is a <b>given</b> - and the real question is <b>if </b>the Grand Inquisitor can get the right amount of allies to make it a short one, <i>instead</i> of long and bloody.<br /> <br /> Neither of these point to a solid status quo in the leadership, imho.<br /> <br /> All of that said, i'll agree with your point that acquisition of territory and with it human herds is critical in the Sabbat's current situation, to recoup past losses if nothing else.<br /> <br /> Anyway, moving on...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what?p=1494169#post1494169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my world, Regent Melinda Galbraith became increasingly erratic and isolated, largely abandoning control of the sect a couple of decades ago and then vanishing entirely. As she become dramatically less interested in ruling, Cathari demagogues mostly gained control over the fractious sect. The Cathari demagogues appealed to the most hedonistic desires of the masses. Under their influence, the Cathari path swelled enormously in numbers, because they raised their shovelheads to True Sabbat status in a tiny fraction of the time of most Paths. They basically raised their shovelheads to True Sabbat status the moment they displayed clear devotion to the Path, ignoring any requirements of military discipline and competence. They also encouraged incredibly reckless, but popular, behavior, essentially turning the Sabbat into a bunch of incompetent psychopathic hedonists.<br /> <br /> This resulted in the loss of considerable amounts of Sabbat territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Galbraith turning erratic and there being no clear sucessor or individual to play power behind the throne could lead to something of a crisis while cardinals, prisci and archbishops all try to make a variety of moves to set either themselves or people they support into such a position, with the Cathari demagogues being simply the first &quot;successful&quot; attempt in that regard.<br /> <br /> The downgrade of quality among the Cathari shouldn't be an issue, at least not in the beginning - they are grunts, leadership is stil the same, so no loss of competence at the top. Except it leads to a boom of population, that puts a greater pressure on maintaning things, that gets even worse if the lion's share of these newbies are a bunch of unruly, pleasure-seeking borderline useless shovelheads.<br /> <br /> They quickly go from reinforcements to liabilities, like every band of barely competent to incompetent greenhorns hastily thrown in a warzone, to the chagrin of veterans that might learn of the degree of unreliability only too late. From there rises vulnerability and the steady fall of Sabbat domains.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1494111-new-orleans-is-the-new-capital-of-the-sabbat-the-cathari-have-been-purged-now-what?p=1494169#post1494169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Montreal was lost. Many blame Cathari incompetence and recklessness for this loss. What has made it much worse is the clumsy propaganda the Cathari demagogues put out afterwards, claiming that this was a good thing, that the Sabbat had evolved beyond the need for territory, and that the Sabbat was more dangerous than ever without territory. This propaganda was so blatantly absurd and such a ridiculous insult to the intelligence of most older Sabbat that it aroused a &quot;let them eat cake&quot; level of F-YOUUUU!!!!! from the followers of more disciplined paths. Only the sheer numbers of the Cathari prevented an immediate civil war.<br /> <br /> The Grand Inquisitor used this widespread hatred to promote her own agenda. She believes the Sabbat should be a disciplined nation and a safe haven for those vampires that reject humanity and desire to advance spiritually on Paths of Enlightenment. As such, it needs to reconquer a reasonably large amount of territory, secure the borders of that territory, and purge those elements that either oppose those two goals, or threaten to cause juicebag stampedes with their idiocy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And if Montreal is gone, chances are that with it went the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Widows\" target=\"_blank\">Widows</a> coven, that were probably one of the strongest challenges to the Demagogues' authority within the Cathari. That explains all too well their stupid attempt to lionize what was a clear loss on material and spiritual levels as a sort of moral victory and springboard for growth i dare say.<br /> <br /> All of that said, the end of Rose and Creamy Jade doesn't have to mean the end of internal disention in their ranks, as many of their followers were not only Montreal locals, meaning their final deaths could make them into martyrs, specially after the Demagogues' cavalier treatment of Montreal's fall.<br /> <br /> So, to sum it up the high level of F-YOUUUU!!!!! might be a thing <b>also </b>among the followers of Cathari, a number that might grow larger among those members who were around before Galbraith's disappearing act and might themselves resent &quot;the new generation&quot;, its behaviour and inexperience to a degree.<br /> <br /> How aware or not kindred from other paths are of these issues could have a big part to play in the ongoing conflict's resolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-08-2023, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T18:14:06-07:00","id":1495465,"title":"","content":"Well, the player pack managed to convince the leadership of the Noddists that the purge of the Cathari was justified. The player characters were each raised to Bishop status as a reward for their loyalty to the Grand Inquisitor, their military success during the siege of New Orleans, and their diplomatic success at convincing the Noddist leadership to back the powergrab by the Grand Inquisitor. And that was the end of the campaign. Really good roleplay all around, especially their arguments as to why the Cathari deserved purging.<br /> <br /> When I created this thread I considered continuing the campaign past this point, but this really turned out to be a satisfying end to the campaign. Thank you all for your advice just the same.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}